  "short_description": "575 Wp Adani ELAN Shine n-type TOPCon bifacial dual-glass module, 22.3% efficient, 144 half-cut cells, 12-yr product and 30-yr power warranty.",
  "long_description": "## What it is\n\nThe Adani Solar ASB-M10-144-575 is a 575 Wp glass-to-glass bifacial module from the ELAN Shine TOPCon Gen-II range, built from 144 half-cut M10 n-type bifacial cells with multi-busbar interconnection. Both faces are glass — 2.0 mm anti-reflective coated high-transmission glass in front, 2.0 mm semi-tempered glass behind — laminated with a high volume-resistivity, low-MVTR encapsulant. At 22.3% module efficiency it is the most efficient of the three flagship panels in this catalogue.\n\n## What it's for\n\nUtility-scale ground-mounted plants and large commercial and industrial rooftops, where the higher efficiency means fewer modules, less structure and less cable for the same plant size. N-type cells hold their output better in the heat of the Deccan summer and carry no light-induced degradation loss, so the first-year drop is smaller than on a P-type module.\n\n## Key specifications\n\nAt STC the module gives 575 Wp at 43.78 V and 13.14 A, with 52.3 V open-circuit and 13.89 A short-circuit. Power tolerance is 0 to +4.99 Wp. Temperature coefficients are −0.32 %/°C on power and −0.24 %/°C on Voc, with NOCT at 45 °C and an operating range of −40 °C to +85 °C. Maximum system voltage is 1500 V and the maximum series fuse rating is 30 A. The laminate is rated for 3600 Pa downward and 1600 Pa upward load at a design safety factor of 1.5. The panel measures 2278 mm × 1133 mm × 30 mm and weighs 33.5 kg. The IP68 junction box feeds 300 mm leads terminated in MC4-compatible connectors. Approvals listed on the datasheet cover IEC 61215, IEC 61730, IEC 61701 salt mist, IEC 62716 ammonia and IEC 60068-2-68 sand and dust, alongside BIS registration.\n\n## Application and installation notes\n\nBolt it through the frame mounting holes or clamp it to the rail, keeping within the 3600 Pa / 1600 Pa load ratings. Note the higher 52.3 V open-circuit voltage — check string length against the 1500 V system limit and against your inverter's cold-morning window. Leave clearance and a light-coloured surface behind the array to collect the rear-side gain. At 33.5 kg it is a two-person lift.\n\n## What's in the box\n\nOne 575 Wp module with junction box, 300 mm leads and MC4-compatible connectors fitted. Structure, clamps, earthing hardware and DC cable are supplied separately. Warranty: 12 years on product, 30 years on performance, with degradation under 1.0% in the first year and under 0.40% a year thereafter, reaching 87.4% of rated power at year 30.",
